lName":"Botnick WC","lastName":"Botnick","firstName":"W C","initials":"WC"},{"fullName":"Burnett B","lastName":"Burnett","firstName":"B","initials":"B"},{"fullName":"Chervu A","lastName":"Chervu","firstName":"A","initials":"A"},{"fullName":"Comerota AJ","lastName":"Comerota","firstName":"A J","initials":"AJ"},{"fullName":"Dy NM","lastName":"Dy","firstName":"N M","initials":"NM"},{"fullName":"Fulco FA","lastName":"Fulco","firstName":"F A","initials":"FA"},{"fullName":"Gossage JR","lastName":"Gossage","firstName":"J R","initials":"JR"},{"fullName":"Kaatz S","lastName":"Kaatz","firstName":"S","initials":"S"},{"fullName":"Lahiri B","lastName":"Lahiri","firstName":"B","initials":"B"},{"fullName":"Lerner RG","lastName":"Lerner","firstName":"R G","initials":"RG"},{"fullName":"Masson JA","lastName":"Masson","firstName":"J A","initials":"JA"},{"fullName":"Moll S","lastName":"Moll","firstName":"S","initials":"S"},{"fullName":"Morganroth M","lastName":"Morganroth","firstName":"M","initials":"M"},{"fullName":"Patel K","lastName":"Patel","firstName":"K","initials":"K"},{"fullName":"Paulson R","lastName":"Paulson","firstName":"R","initials":"R"},{"fullName":"Powell R","lastName":"Powell","firstName":"R","initials":"R"},{"fullName":"Samson R","lastName":"Samson","firstName":"R","initials":"R"},{"fullName":"Seibert A","lastName":"Seibert","firstName":"A","initials":"A"},{"fullName":"Spyropoulos A","lastName":"Spyropoulos","firstName":"A","initials":"A"},{"fullName":"Vrooman PS Jr","lastName":"Vrooman","firstName":"P S","initials":"PS"}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-5577-6808"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-8334-3057"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-9164-4538"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-9419-8772"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-9422-1186"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-1492-9764"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-4227-3256"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-6220-4362"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-6974-9509"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-7795-6022"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-8512-9043"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-9580-8576"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["altmetrics","recommended_reviews","supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"24","volume":"361","journalIssueId":1684252,"dateOfPublication":"2009 Dec","monthOfPublication":12,"yearOfPublication":2009,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"N Engl J Med","title":"The New England journal of medicine","essn":"1533-4406","issn":"0028-4793","isoabbreviation":"N Engl J Med","nlmid":"0255562"},"printPublicationDate":"2009-12-01"},"pubYear":"2009","pageInfo":"2342-2352","abstractText":"<h4>Background</h4>The direct oral thrombin inhibitor dabigatran has a predictable anticoagulant effect and may be an alternative therapy to warfarin for patients who have acute venous thromboembolism.<h4>Methods</h4>In a randomized, double-blind, noninferiority trial involving patients with acute venous thromboembolism who were initially given parenteral anticoagulation therapy for a median of 9 days (interquartile range, 8 to 11), we compared oral dabigatran, administered at a dose of 150 mg twice daily, with warfarin that was dose-adjusted to achieve an international normalized ratio of 2.0 to 3.0. The primary outcome was the 6-month incidence of recurrent symptomatic, objectively confirmed venous thromboembolism and related deaths. Safety end points included bleeding events, acute coronary syndromes, other adverse events, and results of liver-function tests.<h4>Results</h4>A total of 30 of the 1274 patients randomly assigned to receive dabigatran (2.4%), as compared with 27 of the 1265 patients randomly assigned to warfarin (2.1%), had recurrent venous thromboembolism; the difference in risk was 0.4 percentage points (95% confidence interval [CI], -0.8 to 1.5; P<0.001 for the prespecified noninferiority margin). The hazard ratio with dabigatran was 1.10 (95% CI, 0.65 to 1.84). Major bleeding episodes occurred in 20 patients assigned to dabigatran (1.6%) and in 24 patients assigned to warfarin (1.9%) (hazard ratio with dabigatran, 0.82; 95% CI, 0.45 to 1.48), and episodes of any bleeding were observed in 205 patients assigned to dabigatran (16.1%) and 277 patients assigned to warfarin (21.9%; hazard ratio with dabigatran, 0.71; 95% CI, 0.59 to 0.85). The numbers of deaths, acute coronary syndromes, and abnormal liver-function tests were similar in the two groups. Adverse events leading to discontinuation of the study drug occurred in 9.0% of patients assigned to dabigatran and in 6.8% of patients assigned to warfarin (P=0.05).<h4>Conclusions</h4>For the treatment of acute venous thromboembolism, a fixed dose of dabigatran is as effective as warfarin, has a safety profile that is similar to that of warfarin, and does not require laboratory monitoring. (ClinicalTrials.gov number, NCT00291330.)","affiliation":"Department of Medicine, McMaster University and Henderson Research Centre, Hamilton, ON, Canada. schulms@mcmaster.ca","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Comparative Study","Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","Multicenter Study","Randomized Controlled Trial","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Recurrence"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Pyridines","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"AE","qualifierName":"adverse effects"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"TU","qualifierName":"therapeutic use"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Benzimidazoles","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"AE","qualifierName":"adverse effects"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"TU","qualifierName":"therapeutic use"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Warfarin","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"AE","q